# {{PROJECT_NAME}}

A Soroban smart contract scaffolded by [Sorokit](https://github.com/Soro-kiit/soroban-scaffold).

## Template: Basic Counter

This is a minimal learning-friendly counter contract that demonstrates:
- `#![no_std]` Soroban contract structure
- Instance storage via `DataKey` enum
- State mutation: `increment()`, `decrement()`
- State reading: `get_count()`
- Events published on each state change
- Full test suite using Soroban testutils

## Prerequisites

- Rust 1.76+ with `wasm32-unknown-unknown` target
- [Soroban CLI](https://developers.stellar.org/docs/build/smart-contracts/setup) installed

## Build

```bash
cargo build --target wasm32-unknown-unknown --release
```

The optimized WASM will be at:
```
target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/{{PROJECT_NAME}}.wasm
```

## Test

```bash
cargo test
```

## Deploy (Testnet)

```bash
soroban contract deploy \
  --wasm target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/{{PROJECT_NAME}}.wasm \
  --source-account <YOUR_SECRET_KEY> \
  --rpc-url https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org:443 \
  --network-passphrase "Test SDF Network ; September 2015"
```

